The pGCL front end in this package (ast/, check.py, compiler.py, substitute.py, util/ and
__init__.py) and its tests in tests/pgcl come from probably,
https://github.com/Philipp15b/probably (branch brand-new, commit 3db123d), by Philipp Schröer
and contributors, licensed under the Apache License 2.0 (see LICENSE in this folder).

Prodigy changed these files: the imports refer to prodigy.pgcl instead of probably, and the
parts that Prodigy does not use (control-flow graphs, weakest pre-expectations, the command
line) were left out. The pGCL parser (parser.py, util/lark_expr_parser.py) was removed in
v0.6.0 together with the .pgcl syntax; parser.py now only reads .ppy. The git history of
these files records all changes, including those made in probably.
